      "writtenOn": "2023-01-27T22:18:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I realized why I didn\u0027t add it from the beginning. Thing is we don\u0027t add every pages into gcma but only workingset pages. However, the gcma_cc_load_page is supposed to be called for every IO regardless of workingset. It means the hit ratio(i.e., hit / (hit + miss) would be skew on the high used-once pages workload since such pages were never stored from gcma first so keep increasing miss count.\n\nFor the hit ratio, I use (number of loaded pages / number of stored pages) metric.\n\nDo you have any concern or usecase in your mind with the miss counter?",
